# Copy to `.env` or `.env.local` for local dev. For GitHub Pages, inject these as build secrets
# in CI (e.g. GitHub Actions env) so `vite build` bakes them into the bundle.
#
# Sign-in is REQUIRED: the app will not load without Firebase config + Google + allowed domain.

# Allowed Google sign-in domains (after @). Single domain:
# VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=noze.ca
# Or multiple (comma-separated):
# VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=noze.ca,noze.com

# Firebase web app config (Console → Project settings → Your apps → Web)
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456:web:abcdef
# Optional (only if shown in console):
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123456789

# Optional: full URL users land on after clicking "verify email" (must match an authorized domain).
# Defaults to current origin + Vite base. Set explicitly if links must point to production:
# VITE_AUTH_PUBLIC_URL=https://jkandathil.github.io/nozeplot4

# Firebase Console checklist:
# - Authentication → Sign-in method → enable **Google**
# - Authentication → Sign-in method → enable **Email/Password** (for register / email sign-in)
# - Authentication → Templates → edit verification email if desired
# - Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains: add localhost and your GitHub Pages host (e.g. jkandathil.github.io)

# --- GitHub Actions deploy (optional) ---
# Repo: Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions — add the VITE_FIREBASE_* secrets above.
# Workflow: .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml sets VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=noze.ca so only *@noze.ca
# can use the app after Google (or email) sign-in. Push to `main` deploys to branch `gh-pages`.

# Security note: The client checks email domain after Google returns a verified account.
# Determined users could bypass a pure SPA check; for stricter control use Firebase Blocking Functions
# or a small backend that verifies the ID token and enforces domain server-side.
